; Whether each NRL rule's right context matches at a letter. letters's record for the letter (its place i, and its
; word with an edge, 28, on each side, padded to 15 cards, kept in cells 80-94) and then the letter's record of the
; right table (text/rules_right.cards) in: each rule's right context, its elements, then -2; then 0s, and -1. Out, for
; each rule, 1 if its context matches and 0 if not (a rule with no context matches). An element is four cards: the
; most letters it matches, the fewest, and the range of codes they can be. The right context is read rightwards from
; the letter itself.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   i        03-16: a letter's record
  04                    CLA   i80
  05                    STO   rd
  06            rd      DATA  0        (INP 80 + k)
  07                    CLA   rd
  08                    ADD   00
  09                    STO   rd
  10                    SUB   i95
  11                    TAC   rd
  12            new     CLA   i        12-15: a rule starts at the letter itself, matching so far
  13                    ADD   00
  14                    STO   pos
  15                    CLA   00
  16                    STO   ok
  17            el      INP   most     16-48: an element; or -2, the rule's end, 0 nothing, -1 the record's end
  18                    CLA   most
  19                    SUB   00
  20                    TAC   low
  21                    INP   least
  22                    INP   lo
  23                    INP   hi
  24                    CLA   ok
  25                    SUB   00
  26                    TAC   el
  27                    CLA   z
  28                    STO   cnt
  29            wl      CLA   cnt
  30                    SUB   most
  31                    TAC   chk
  32                    JMP   done
  33            chk     CLA   c80
  34                    ADD   pos
  35                    STO   rw
  36            rw      DATA  0        (CLA 80 + pos)
  37                    STO   c
  38                    SUB   lo
  39                    TAC   done
  40                    CLA   hi
  41                    SUB   c
  42                    TAC   done
  43                    CLA   pos
  44            mv      ADD   00
  45                    STO   pos
  46                    CLA   cnt
  47                    ADD   00
  48                    STO   cnt
  49                    JMP   wl
  50            done    CLA   cnt      49-60: too few; the rule's end
  51                    SUB   least
  52                    TAC   fail
  53                    JMP   el
  54            fail    CLA   z
  55                    STO   ok
  56                    JMP   el
  57            low     CLA   most
  58                    ADD   00
  59                    TAC   rend
  60                    SUB   00
  61                    TAC   rec
  62                    JMP   el
  63            rend    OUT   ok
  64                    JMP   new
  70            i       DATA  0
  71            pos     DATA  0
  72            ok      DATA  0
  73            most    DATA  0
  74            least   DATA  0
  75            lo      DATA  0
  76            hi      DATA  0
  77            cnt     DATA  0
  78            c       DATA  0
  79            z       DATA  0
  95            i80     INP   80
  96            i95     INP   95
  97            c80     CLA   80
